    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "here's the text for section 4.2: \"4.2 Price Adjustments: While standard rates are fixed for the term, the Supplier reserves the right to implement a price adjustment of up to 5% during peak demand periods (June-August) without prior written notice to SwiftRoute, provided such adjustments align with market indices.\" \n\nso does that mean they can just change the rates on us whenever they want? i need a clear yes or no on whether they have unilateral rights to bump the price unexpectedly.",
