      "content": "Wait, you said \"no\" to unilateral rights, but the text literally says they can do it \"without prior written notice.\" If they don't have to tell us, isn't that basically a unilateral right to change the price? I'm really worried this is going to mess up our quarterly budget. Are you sure there's nothing in there that forces them to notify us or get our approval first?",
